{
  "statement": "Trustworthiness is essential for maintaining security and privacy in the bookkeeping system. I support all my requirements as they collectively ensure robust protection against unauthorized access and data breaches. However, I recognize the conflicts with SAF-03 and RES-01 regarding audit trail retention. I propose a synthesis where we maintain the 7-year retention requirement but also ensure compliance with necessary regulations, allowing for flexibility in how the audit trail can be stored or accessed after the 5-year mark. Additionally, I suggest we explore options to optimize TRU-06's logging delay to align better with EFF-07 without compromising security.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-03", "RES-01"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "TRU-03's requirement for a minimum 5-year audit trail conflicts with SAF-03's requirement for retaining records for at least 7 years, and may also conflict with RES-01 if regulations require longer retention."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-07"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "TRU-06's requirement for logging user access with a maximum delay of 1 second may compete with EFF-07's operational efficiency goal, potentially impacting performance."
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
